{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"1f013f6426b27f8cb555c22229b6c039f0c3bf25e128f377b49ae37cdbaeeacb","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira reconcile-bridge comment sync","key_entities":["REB-1861","REB-1580","REB-1829","comment_ids","RECONCILER_MARKER","outbound_comments._normalize_comment_body","_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX","irongrey-chubby-oxpecker","bd80-0603-7d44-4d9f","reconcile-bridge.yml","712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e"],"problem_keywords":["duplicate comments","jira comment cleanup","reconciliation loop","bot-authored spam","comment deduplication"],"propositions":["The Jira reconcile-bridge reposted duplicate comments on every hourly pass due to inert PRIMARY comment-id dedup (empty comment_ids map), affecting ~30 issues and causing REB-1861 to reach Jira's 5000-comment hard cap.","Phase-1 cleanup deleted 29,931 marked bot-authored duplicate comments across 27 issues by keeping only the oldest copy per distinct normalized body (using outbound_comments._normalize_comment_body), with marker detection performed on pre-strip rendered ADF text to filter candidates.","Post-deletion verification across all 30 issues confirmed zero missing distinct bodies, unchanged non-candidate comment counts, and REB-1861 reduced from 5000 to 79 comments, with independent backup-vs-live diff confirming the invariant that every distinct body retains exactly one surviving instance.","Phase-2 cleanup (836 truncation-suffix bot comments in REB-1567, REB-1931, REB-2605) was deliberately not executed; these comments lack the marker paragraph because outbound truncation at 32767 chars cut it off, and deletion requires separate operator decision behind --include-truncated flag.","The reconcile-bridge workflow remains paused (disabled_manually) for the entire operation and was not re-enabled; the root defect (aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615, change 1957) is fixed but the duplicate set is now static."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787729116334466001,"uuid":"2338598a-93aa-4daa-a3f0-134c61ecac94"}